From 5e1ea841c743713498733e06985f59f48b6d0d6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:10:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dri: round up the subsampled plane size on dma-buf import

When a planar YUV dma-buf with an odd width or height is imported, the
subsampled planes are created with the size shifted down, one chroma
sample short of what the producer allocated. This results in the
information loss. This contradics with the other code handling
dimensions. FOr example, util_format_get_plane_width/height() rounds up.
In the kernel, drm_format_info_plane_width/height() also rounds
dimensions up.

Round the plane size up, as util_format_get_plane_width() and DRM do.

Fixes: ecd6fce2611e ("mesa/st: support lowering multi-planar YUV")
Cc: mesa-stable
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45727>
(cherry picked from commit 6b41b56dea2d3d827cbb118ece95e2ba39a73e1a)
Link: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/commit/5e1ea841c743713498733e06985f59f48b6d0d6a
[ adapted: dropped .pick_status.json, not in the 26.3.0 tarball or bookkeeping only ]
---
 .pick_status.json                | 2 +-
 src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c
index 4846d9c1c7e7..b8b732c2bd8f 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c
@@ -750,8 +750,8 @@ dri_create_image_from_winsys(struct dri_screen *screen,
       struct pipe_resource *tex;
 
       templ.next = img->texture;
-      templ.width0 = width >> map->planes[i].width_shift;
-      templ.height0 = height >> map->planes[i].height_shift;
+      templ.width0 = DIV_ROUND_UP(width, 1 << map->planes[i].width_shift);
+      templ.height0 = DIV_ROUND_UP(height, 1 << map->planes[i].height_shift);
       if (use_lowered)
          templ.format = map->planes[i].dri_format;
       else
